{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>If he betrays her</b> — twenty times in the Masorah, this one. And the other: ותתפשהו בכגדו (and she shall seize him by his cloak), and that is what R. Elazar said: once he spread his cloak over her, he is no longer permitted to sell her, for we learn it from בגדו there, which is an actual garment. And R. Akiva too, who holds once he betrayed her he is no longer permitted to sell her, and expounds בבגדו as the language of betrayal (בגידה) — he too learns בגד there from here, for there too was betrayal, for he holds like the one who says he entered to attend to his needs but the likeness of his father appeared to him."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {0 "The phrase 'twenty times in the Masorah' refers to the root בגד appearing with this spelling; the second occurrence cited is Genesis 39:12. The closing passage alludes to the Talmudic dispute (Sotah 36b) regarding Joseph and Potiphar's wife."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:13:51.663299895Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}